<Base title="About" section="about" description="Ege Ipek: auditor of emissions data under the EU ETS and CBAM. Record, standards, independence.">
  <h1 class="big">About</h1>

  <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px">I audit emissions data under the EU ETS and CBAM as a freelance verifier in the pool of an accredited verification body; first assignments are scheduled for the 2027 cycle. I also take consulting subcontracts from CBAM and ETS advisory firms. From 2022 to 2025 I managed installation-level monitoring, reporting and filing for industrial carbon-offset projects at ClimeCo in New York.</p>

  <section class="facts">
    <dl>
      <dt>Verification</dt>
      <dd>Trained and examined as an EU ETS and CBAM verifier within an accredited body's freelance pool, 2026. Activity groups: chemicals, metals. Verification opinions are issued by the body, not by me.</dd>

      <dt>Operator-side MRV</dt>
      <dd>ClimeCo, Senior Associate, January 2022 to August 2025, New York. Monitoring plans, data cycles and filings for industrial projects registered with the Climate Action Reserve: nitrous-oxide abatement, low-carbon cement and supplementary cementitious materials, carbon capture and storage. Registry IDs available on request.</dd>

      <dt>Methodology work</dt>
      <dd>Contributions to the Climate Action Reserve's Low-Carbon Cement Protocol and its China adipic-acid adaptation; edits to an Isometric CCS methodology; a crediting methodology begun for CO₂-mineralised aggregate.</dd>

      <dt>Education</dt>
      <dd>MS Environmental and Green Chemistry, George Washington University, 2021. BS Chemistry, 2020.</dd>

      <dt>Standards</dt>
      <dd>Regulation (EU) 2018/2066 (MRR) and 2018/2067 (AVR); Regulation (EU) 2023/956 as amended by 2025/2083, with Implementing Regulations 2025/2546 and 2025/2547 and Delegated Regulation 2025/2551; ISO 14065, ISO/IEC 17029, ISO 14064-3.</dd>

      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>Turkish (native), English, French. German in progress.</dd>

      <dt>Location</dt>
      <dd>Berlin. Registered as a freelance natural person (freiberuflich).</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="rulebox">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Independence</h2>
    <p>Verification and consulting are kept apart. I do not verify any installation I have advised, and I disclose consulting relationships to the verification body that contracts me, as its conflict-of-interest procedure requires. Nothing on this site presents the two as one offer.</p>
    <p>This site expresses the views of none of the organisations I work with.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="rulebox">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What this site is</h2>
    <p>A working record. Notes are numbered, dated and carry a status. A finding works one question to a resolution. A position states my reading of a live rule as of its date, and stays up when superseded. An explainer sets out a method. Instruments are tools I built for my own scoping, published as they stand.</p>
    <p>No entry describes a client engagement.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
